Native ARM (a.out) C runtime for DiscoBSD/GBA - crt0 + minimal libc, built by
this port's own toolchain (smlrc -> as_arm -> ld_arm). Prototype; not yet wired
into a lib Makefile. See sys/arch/gba/NOTES.toolchain section 11.

crt0.s  - _start: environ=envp; call main(argc,argv,envp); _exit(). ARM, links
          at an even address so ISA-aware exec (syscall.c) enters ARM state.
clib.s  - syscalls via the simulated-SWI trampoline at 0x03006400: write, read,
          open, close, lseek, _exit/exit, _brk; sbrk (uses _end/_curbrk); errno;
          __aeabi_uidiv/idiv/uidivmod/idivmod (repeated subtraction - correct,
          slow; avoids instructions as_arm doesn't yet emit, e.g. flag-setting
          S-suffix / tst). Only as_arm-supported instructions are used.

Build one native ARM a.out and run it:
  ./build.sh                              # builds as_arm ld_arm smlrc-arm (parent)
  ./smlrc-arm rt/hello.c hello.s
  ./as_arm -o hello.o hello.s
  ./as_arm -o crt0.o rt/crt0.s
  ./as_arm -o clib.o rt/clib.s
  ./ld_arm -e _start -o hello.out crt0.o hello.o clib.o     # OMAGIC a.out (GBA)
  python3 rt/run_omagic.py hello.out       # load like the kernel, run in Unicorn
  # (ld_arm -b ... = flat image for rt/run_rt.py instead)

Validated in Unicorn (emulated syscall trampoline): hello.c prints its string;
num.c prints numbers via division/modulo/recursion. hello.out/num.out are real
OMAGIC/MID=0 a.out executables (a_entry even = ARM, load base 0x02001800) that
the GBA kernel can exec (needs the ISA-aware-exec kernel, commit 0e9de6f).

NEEDS for on-hardware use: put a built .out into the userland SD/ROM image and
run it from the shell; a proper lib Makefile to build crt0.o + a libc.a with
the native tools; more libc (printf, string, malloc) as smlrc coverage grows.

--- libc.c (item 2: C library, compiled by smlrc) ---
libc.c: string (strlen/strcmp/strcpy/strchr/memcpy/memset), stdlib (atoi),
stdio (putchar/puts/printf). printf supports %d %u %x %c %s %% and uses varargs
- the SmallerC stack-based va model matches cgarm's frame (r0-r3 spilled
contiguously to [fp+8..20], stack args at [fp+24+]), so it Just Works.
Build: smlrc-arm libc.c libc.s; as_arm -o libc.o libc.s. Link libc.o + clib.o.
LIMITATION: a call with >4 args errors (cgarm errorInternal 200), so printf is
limited to fmt + <=3 varargs until item 4 (>4-arg AAPCS stack passing) lands -
that is the key unlock for full printf. Validated in Unicorn AND on the real
kernel via mgbarun (a printf program auto-run at boot printed correctly).
Still TODO for item 2: malloc/free (bump allocator over sbrk), more string/
ctype/stdio as needed.
